            tabindex="0"
            role="img"
            aria-label="Session one timeline over 20 minutes. Child A, neurotypical, explores freely, finds creature 1 and signals at minute 7, finds creature 2 and repeats the signal rapidly at minute 12, then keeps exploring the map. Child B, with ADHD, moves more slowly, is first to try the signal after a cue at minute 3, notices A and joins the signal at minute 8, gets stuck on a bug three times between minutes 9 and 11 and asks to switch games, then watches and joins the second activation at minute 14. Interaction moves from solo to parallel play at minute 8 and again from minute 14."
          >
